think With the DRIVE family whole at ALES83, the plainest step beside it is the even-harmonic complement to its odd clippers: the full-wave rectifier, y = |x|. Lindy (rectification is the oldest even-harmonic move in analog electronics); crux-first (|−x| = |x| is the purest even map, exact everywhere but one sample).
think The one genuine edge: |sample_min| = 32768 overflows the i16 positive rail, so that lone sample saturates to sample_max rather than wrapping. Computed the magnitude in i64 so negating sample_min never overflows before the pin — timeline.saturate does honest work here (unlike ALES83, where the decimator only copies existing samples).
think Named it as the purest even map (no gain, no ceiling, no resolution — only a span), so it carries exactly one fault, BadRange. Memoryless, idempotent (a non-negative sample rectifies to itself), and always non-negative — the one-sided signal is the point.
obs Followed the sibling pattern exactly (crush.rye, tube.rye, decimate.rye): module + design doc + witness + README status-line sync + session log, one signed commit. Seven laws proven in the selftest; witness GREEN; tame_style_check clean; width clean.
